+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+GraphHelm's install documentation currently claims platform verification only for Windows x86-64
+and Ubuntu x86-64 (the two `v0.1.0` release archives), and routes everyone else — including
+Windows 11 on ARM64 (e.g., Snapdragon laptops) — to "build from source" with no recorded proof
+that the build actually succeeds or runs on that hardware. Windows on ARM is a mainstream laptop
+class today; users on it get no answer for whether `graphhelm` installs and runs natively. This
+change verifies that promise once, on real Snapdragon hardware, and records the result so the
+documentation can claim it.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Perform a one-time installation rehearsal of the `graphhelm` CLI on a Windows 11 ARM64
+  (aarch64, Snapdragon) laptop using the documented source path
+  (`cargo +1.97.1 install --locked --path apps/cli`), and confirm `graphhelm --version` prints
+  `graphhelm 0.1.0` from the installed binary on PATH.
+- Add a dated acceptance record under `docs/acceptance/` following the existing transcript format
+  (`docs/acceptance/install-rehearsal-2026-09-13.md`): host identification (SoC/OS/version), the
+  commit under test, and the command transcript with outputs.
+- Update `docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md` §1 so that Windows ARM64 appears as a verified
+  platform (verified from source, with a pointer to the acceptance record), alongside the existing
+  verified-archive claim.
+- Record any prerequisite gap discovered during the rehearsal (for example, the Windows
+  prerequisites block does not list the MSVC linker Build Tools) in the acceptance record; a
+  matching fix to the prerequisites text in `docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md` is included only if
+  the rehearsal actually hit the gap.
+
+No code, schema, dependency, or release-archive changes. No new archive is added to the `v0.1.0`
+release table (`docs/releases/0.1.0.md` stays as is: it documents the shipped archives, and there
+is no `windows-aarch64` archive in this change).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `install/verified-platforms`: which platforms are claimed as verified for installing and running
+  the `graphhelm` CLI, how each claim must be evidenced (checked-in acceptance record naming the
+  host hardware, commit, and transcript), and the rule that a platform may not be listed until its
+  observer has been run on native hardware (emulation, VMs, and cross-compilation are not
+  observers). This capability owns the platform-verification claims of the install documentation
+  going forward.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+(None — `openspec/specs/` is empty; this change introduces the first capability.)
+
+## Impact
+
+- Documentation: `docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md` (verified-platforms statement in §1; possibly
+  the Windows prerequisites block), plus one new file under `docs/acceptance/`.
+- Evidence host: a Windows 11 ARM64 (aarch64, Snapdragon) laptop must be available at apply time.
+  The machine used for this planning checkout is AMD64 (Windows 11 Pro, AMD Ryzen 9 9950X), so the
+  hardware observer cannot be run from here — see `design.md` for the consequence (an apply run
+  without the laptop ends `OBSERVER_MISSING` rather than claiming verification).
+- No effect on code, CI (hosted CI is intentionally disabled in this repository), dependencies,
+  schemas, or the release artifacts of `v0.1.0`.
